      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-225340",
      ":question/problem": "Let $a, b \u2208 Z$. Prove that $5a\u22615b(mod7)$ if $a\u2261b(mod7)$.\n\nSince $a\u2261b(mod7)$, by the definition of {{field-1}}, $7\u2223(a - b)$ {{field-2}} {{field-3}}\nfor some integer $k$.Now, multiplying both sides of $a - b =$ {{field-4}} by {{field-5}}, we get\n$5$ {{field-6}} {{field-7}} {{field-8}} {{field-9}} {{field-10}}\nwhere $m = 5k$ is an integer. According to the definition of {{field-11}}, the final equation implies that\n$5a\u22615b(mod7)$."
